-- title:
--   Tame finite vertex stabilisers on the Bruhat–Tits tree
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a_1,b_1$, a nonzero squarefree $N$, primes $q,q'\ge 5$ with $q'\ne q$ and $q,q'\nmid N$, and primes $r,\bar r\ge 5$ with $\bar r\ne r$ and $r,\bar r\nmid N$, and assume $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and that, for a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division ring exactly when $\bar r\in v$. Let $\Lambda_1$ be a maximal order (an order not properly contained in another order), $R_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders, of relative index $N$ in one of them) with $R_1\le\Lambda_1$, and $n_1$ a finite-idele unit in `primeHeckeSet R₁ r` such that `meetOrder R₁ n₁` $=R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$, is fixed by conjugation by $n_1$, and such that shifting twice by $n_1$ acts trivially on its class set, both class sets involved being finite. Let $A_2$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $r$ a non-unit, $v_2$ a height-one prime containing $r$, $\iota_2$ an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ into $2\times2$ matrices over $C_A=$[`ValuationSubring.ratClosure A₂`](def/ValuationSubring_CompletionRatClosure.html#L13), and $\rho_2:\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^\times\to\mathrm{PGL}_2(C_A)$ the induced projective representation. Further data $s_2,sf_2$ indexed by the primes $\ell\ne q,q'$ satisfy the frame conditions summarised here: $sf_2(\ell)$ equals $s_2(\ell)\otimes 1$ away from $r$ and $1$ above $r$, the product of the diagonal image of $\ell$ with $sf_2(\ell)^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell\mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_2(\ell))=\ell$. Finally $R_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $C_A$, with finite residue field, whose image in $C_A$ consists of the elements of valuation at most $1$; $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^\times$ acts on the vertices (homothety classes of full $R_0$-lattices in $C_A^2$) through $\rho_2$, preserving adjacency in `BruhatTits.tree R₀ C_A`. The conclusion is twofold: for every vertex $w$, the stabiliser of $w$ in the image under $\rho_2$ of `awayUnits R₁ v₂` (the units of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ whose image at each height-one prime $u\ne v_2$ lies in the group generated by the local box units of $R_1$ at $u$) is finite, its cardinality is not divisible by $r$, and the valuation of that cardinality in the completion of $A_2$'s valuation equals $1$; and the same three assertions hold, for every prime $\ell\ne q,q'$ and every vertex $w$, with $R_1$ replaced by $R_1\cap sf_2(\ell)R_1sf_2(\ell)^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the tameness input for the Čerednik–Drinfeld side of the argument: vertex stabilisers of the groups of $r$-units acting on the Bruhat–Tits tree at $r$ are finite of order prime to $r$, hence of order a unit in the relevant valuation. It is used by the statements about `evenAwayUnits` that feed the equivariant Mumford–Kurihara uniformisation of the quotients of Drinfeld's $\Omega$, where finiteness and tameness of stabilisers are required.
